Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON  21 AUG 01 at 14 20 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on core biopsy done at an outside hospital  not reviewed her  dense calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   1  TWO SETS OF STITCHES   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH RARE MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  BREAST  LEFT   2  ONE SET OF STITCHES   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  G   WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF A BLUE INKED MARGIN  SIDE OPPOSITE OF THE ASPECT WITH A STITCH   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  LEFT   3   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  24 AUG 01 at 15 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  are two specimens  The first specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm breast tissue fragment with a long stitch designating the lateral margin and a short stitch designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  superior blue  inferior green  posterior black  anterior red  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from lateral to medial in cassettes A F  Also in the same container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm specimen with a stitch designating the margin furthest away from calcium  The specimen is inked as follows  margin furthest away from calcium black  opposite side blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes G H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  3  is a unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tissue specimen which is black inked and submitted entirely in cassettes I L  Resident  HEIKE VARNHOLT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   1  PART B  BREAST  LEFT   2  PART C  BREAST  LEFT  3  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN ONE SMALL FOCUS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white stellate firm nodule abutting the inked margin  A representative section of the tumor and margin is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette H  The lesion is submitted entirely in cassettes A   C  Representative sections of the remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes D   G  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST LESION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
